WEBVTT

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:07.940
After Colony 196.

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:13.110
Colony L3 X-18999 has
proclaimed independence.

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:16.160
The leader’s name is
Mariemaia Khushrenada.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.910
The daughter of Treize.

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:21.620
Upon abducting Relena…

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:25.320
…Mariemaia declares war on
the Earth Sphere Unified Nation.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:27.290
And behind the scenes…

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:32.260
…the Gundam pilots are
fiercely battling each other.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.920
He’s pretty good.

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:39.310
Hey, I know this…

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:41.510
I know this style of combat!

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:47.770
No question!

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:49.570
Trowa’s in that suit!

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:51.030
Damn it!

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:10.750
I’ve always wanted
to fight you like this!

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:22.310
At this rate, it’ll take us
five more days to rendezvous…

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:24.140
…with the resources disposal
satellite.

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:26.810
We could reduce the time…

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:29.650
…by up to eighty hours
on this route.

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:31.150
Great!

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:32.690
Then, let’s take that route!

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:35.650
But considering the fuel
needed to accelerate now…

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:38.200
…and decelerate at the
rendezvous point…

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:41.240
…we’d have no propulsion
by the time we got there.

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:43.620
Then there’s no way
to get back?

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:46.250
No, there’s a way to get back.

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:48.960
If we detonated the power
generator…

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:50.670
…and used the explosion
as our propulsion…

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:53.090
…we could return to Earth
in no time.

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:55.670
We’d fly the ship to Venus…

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:58.760
…and use the catapult effect
of its gravity to get to Earth.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:01.890
Our main problem is the time
we have at the rendezvous point.

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:03.640
According to calculations…

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:06.730
…this ship’ll run alongside the
satellite for only five seconds!

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:10.230
How many people we can
get on in five seconds?

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:12.910
Some danger can’t be avoided.

00:02:12.910 --> 00:02:15.530
Since Duo’s scheduled message
hasn’t arrived…

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:18.910
…it’s likely that things are
getting more difficult there.

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:20.740
Then it’s decided.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:23.790
Our satellite team will consist
of Abdul, myself, and…

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:26.250
No, I’ll be going alone.

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:27.330
Master Quatre!

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:30.530
Please, take us with you!

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:33.630
Rashid, start the booster
one last time.

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:39.220
Each of us is ready to give
up his life for you, anytime!

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:45.390
In this universe, nothing is
more precious than life.

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:48.340
Sandrock made that clear to me.

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:54.820
Self-detonation device?

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:55.900
That’s right.

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:57.990
It’s been installed in Sandrock.

00:02:57.990 --> 00:02:59.710
For confidentiality?

00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:01.610
No, that’s not why.

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:04.370
It’s because those with power
must be prepared…

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:06.240
…to lose their lives.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:08.370
I don’t quite understand.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:10.080
I guess not.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:12.370
You don’t need to understand
just yet.

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:14.880
An order from the organization?

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:15.710
Yeah.

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:18.250
But forget this thing!

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:20.380
Quatre.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:22.680
Fight as your heart tells you.

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:26.970
And use the self-detonation
device…

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:29.340
…only when you feel
you must.

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:30.680
Yes.

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:42.740
I can’t take away his
kindness and purity.

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:48.240
Although this may end up being
a crueler destiny for him…

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:49.750
…than Operation Meteor.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:59.670
Operation Meteor

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:08.350
What’s going on, Wufei?!

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:10.270
Are you guys doing
the right thing?

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:11.060
What?!

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:19.430
I’m asking if you guys
are doing the right thing!

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:26.450
Wufei!

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:27.620
Hit the self-detonation switch!

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:45.010
I repeat…

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:46.340
Hit the switch.

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:57.280
T-Trowa.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:59.460
Why have you betrayed us?!

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:00.820
Got the wrong guy.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:02.690
I’m not Trowa.

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:06.110
You’re not serious!?

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:14.740
So this’ll end everything?!

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:46.650
This’ll end everything.

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:50.880
What happened?!

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:52.790
Why won’t it explode?!

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:54.660
What did I do wrong?!

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:55.910
Duo!

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:02.170
Deathscythe is a superb
piece of art!

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:05.370
Think of a better way,
rather than destroying it.

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:09.790
I won’t let my buddy be
used for mass destruction!

00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:15.270
So you were planning
to kill me…

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:17.350
…after you destroyed Deathscythe.

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:19.060
I was gonna kill everyone here.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:20.810
Including myself.

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:22.570
If it meant peace
for this Colony…

00:06:22.570 --> 00:06:24.730
…I’d be the God of Death
any day.

00:06:24.730 --> 00:06:27.900
If you’d go that far,
then try and outwit me.

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:29.160
What?

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:31.780
Duo, steal Deathscythe!

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:32.660
Huh?!

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:34.790
Forget Operation Meteor!

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:37.210
Take it to the Earth now.

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:40.630
There’s a man called Howard
on the Pacific Ocean.

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:42.420
You can rely on him.

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:45.130
Of course, go as
the God of Death.

00:06:46.650 --> 00:06:48.590
The God of Death.

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:52.250
It’s a lot better than being
the hero of a massacre.

00:07:05.330 --> 00:07:07.150
I am not Trowa.

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:09.950
I’m a nameless soldier
who’s been on the battlefield…

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:11.660
…for as long as I remember.

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:20.620
The first time I met
the man called Trowa…

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:23.290
…I was helping with
adjustments to Heavyarms.

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:25.630
What’s this all about?

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:28.700
Why are we limiting all
our attacks to OZ?!

00:07:28.700 --> 00:07:31.130
If we proceeded with
Operation Meteor…

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:33.430
…two billion people will die.

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:35.970
Don’t you think this is going
too far for revenge…

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:37.350
…for Heero Yuy, huh?

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:40.020
The purpose of this plan
is not revenge!

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:42.520
The plan is for the colonies
to conquer Earth…

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:45.930
…for the awakening
of a “new mankind”!

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:48.030
That sounds like something…

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:50.450
…Dekim of the Barton
Foundation would dream up.

00:07:50.450 --> 00:07:51.240
I see.

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:54.160
You guys have something
against that?

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:57.990
You’re jealous that my father
and the Barton Foundation…

00:07:57.990 --> 00:07:59.870
…will rule the Earth Sphere.

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:01.790
Where are you going, Trowa?!

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:03.620
To tell this to my father.

00:08:05.270 --> 00:08:06.880
Just watch me.

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:11.080
I’ll proceed with Operation
Meteor by myself, if I must.

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:17.720
Now you’ve done it.

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:18.950
I’m sorry.

00:08:18.950 --> 00:08:21.340
But I have family on Earth…

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:24.880
Who’s there?!

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:26.700
I have no name.

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:29.070
If you like, call me “No-Name”.

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:31.690
You saw us?!

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:34.070
I’ll understand if you
want to kill me.

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:36.230
But I might retaliate.

00:08:36.230 --> 00:08:37.070
Don’t.

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:39.700
They’ll find out about
this sooner or later.

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:42.970
There’s no use trying
to hide the facts.

00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:44.960
You’re giving up too easily.

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:46.130
What?

00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:49.210
I was feeling insecure
without a name.

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:51.590
I wouldn’t mind taking
on his name.

00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:53.940
What are you talking about?

00:08:53.940 --> 00:08:56.970
I seem to be best suited
for the battlefields.

00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:00.930
Are you saying you’ll pilot
this suit, Heavyarms?

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:03.480
I like this suit.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:06.520
But I have no interest
in conquering Earth.

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:10.940
Alright.

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:13.990
As of this moment, your
name is Trowa Barton.

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:17.570
You are now in charge
of Operation Meteor!

00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:20.480
I understand.

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:53.640
Trowa…

00:09:56.670 --> 00:09:59.610
Couldn’t he have taken things
a little easier?

00:10:13.650 --> 00:10:15.970
The Taurus troops ahead…

00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:18.300
…are heading toward
the relay station.

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:20.010
They’re taking a roundabout
route.

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:22.310
But their destination
is still Earth.

00:10:23.280 --> 00:10:26.730
A Preventer cruiser will arrive
from the Lunar Base shortly.

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:29.900
I’m sure we can buy some
time when they arrive.

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:32.260
Any word from Heero
and Duo?

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:34.890
Really…

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:36.400
Sally.

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:39.490
Did you confirm any new suit
models in the last battle?

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:40.570
No.

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:44.030
Come to think of it, they were
all Taurus and Space Leos.

00:10:44.430 --> 00:10:46.610
We’ve underestimated them.

00:10:47.720 --> 00:10:49.830
The heat detector shows nothing.

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:52.790
So those troops consisted
primarily of mobile dolls!

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:53.590
Right.

00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:56.420
That means the main troops
with the new mobile suits…

00:10:56.420 --> 00:10:57.720
…are deployed elsewhere.

00:10:57.720 --> 00:10:59.510
Quite an elaborate operation.

00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:01.640
Then where could the
main troops be?

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:03.890
In any case, we’ll leave this area!

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:05.770
Contact Earth at once!

00:11:05.770 --> 00:11:07.130
Roger!

00:11:27.010 --> 00:11:31.450
These people have no idea
what Mariemaia will do to them.

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:39.550
But with the world’s lack
of strength to retaliate…

00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:42.690
…she won’t need five minutes
to take political control.

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:46.300
What would you do in
this situation, Treize?

00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:53.410
We found the resources
disposal satellite.

00:11:53.410 --> 00:11:56.730
We’ve got about three hours
before we reach the satellite.

00:12:08.340 --> 00:12:10.910
My calculations are accurate.

00:12:10.910 --> 00:12:13.120
Unlike those of Quinze.

00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:24.720
So what if you rule
the Earth Sphere?

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:27.720
Are you sure you’d be
carrying on Treize’s…

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:29.970
…I mean, your father’s will
by doing this?

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:31.730
You’ve got it wrong.

00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:33.980
I just want to be victorious.

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:36.020
Then you’ll have to decide…

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:38.970
…on your own, the deeper
meaning of fighting.

00:12:38.970 --> 00:12:40.290
Relena.

00:12:40.290 --> 00:12:42.650
Don’t make me repeat myself.

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:45.310
I won’t allow such rude
comments.

00:12:51.510 --> 00:12:53.290
We can’t catch that.

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:56.330
They’re heading toward
the Space Port.

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:59.300
They seem to be in a rush
for people going to Earth.

00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:01.460
That’s because they’re
gonna escape.

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:02.850
Escape?

00:13:02.850 --> 00:13:05.960
Then why did they bother
to take over this place?

00:13:07.950 --> 00:13:09.220
Come on!

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:12.330
Remember, she is Treize’s
daughter after all.

00:13:12.330 --> 00:13:15.350
I’m more concerned about
the man known as Dekim.

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:17.980
The name Dekim Barton
rings a bell…

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:19.940
They can’t be serious!

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:22.360
They’re planning to go ahead
with Operation Meteor?

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:23.940
Yeah.

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:26.730
But I’ll do everything
I can to stop them.

00:13:32.680 --> 00:13:33.870
<i>Master Quatre.</i>

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:36.170
<i>We’ll reach the resources
disposal satellite…</i>

00:13:36.170 --> 00:13:37.330
<i>…in twenty seconds.</i>

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:38.630
All right.

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:42.540
<i>If it looks too dangerous,
return to the ship at once.</i>

00:13:43.110 --> 00:13:44.320
Yeah.

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:45.710
It’s here!

00:13:58.080 --> 00:14:00.100
<i>Commencing countdown!</i>

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:04.190
<i>Seven, six, five…</i>

00:14:04.370 --> 00:14:06.860
Four… three… two…

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:09.280
<i>One… zero!</i>

00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:24.080
Master Quatre!

00:14:30.400 --> 00:14:32.220
<i>I’m… I’m okay.</i>

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:34.720
<i>I’ve managed to arrive
on the satellite.</i>

00:14:36.870 --> 00:14:38.690
Take care, everyone.

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:41.400
<i>Say hi to the Goddess
on Venus.</i>

00:14:51.670 --> 00:14:53.780
The air remaining on the ship…

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:55.790
…has minimized the rise
in temperatures.

00:14:55.790 --> 00:14:59.330
But it’s still hotter than
a desert in here.

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:06.220
Hi.

00:15:06.220 --> 00:15:07.960
So we meet again.

00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:19.950
The Preventer cruiser has
changed course.

00:15:19.950 --> 00:15:21.770
They’ve realized what’s
happening.

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:23.360
But it’s too late!

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:26.070
By the time they arrive at this
natural resources satellite…

00:15:26.070 --> 00:15:28.940
…the ruler of Earth Sphere
will have changed already.

00:15:28.940 --> 00:15:31.030
Send out the Serpent troops,
at once!

00:15:31.030 --> 00:15:32.110
Yes, sir.

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:34.480
Open the gate on Earth’s side!

00:15:46.060 --> 00:15:48.010
Unidentified mobile suit ahead!

00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:49.260
What?!

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:51.730
Checking the model of
the mobile suit.

00:15:51.730 --> 00:15:53.300
It’s the Tallgeese!

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:55.090
Treize?

00:15:55.090 --> 00:15:56.060
No.

00:15:56.060 --> 00:15:57.700
It must be Zechs.

00:15:57.700 --> 00:15:59.760
The Tallgeese is coming for us!

00:16:25.560 --> 00:16:27.900
My hunch was correct.

00:16:27.900 --> 00:16:29.550
I guess there’s still a place…

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:32.010
…for a man who can’t
get used to peace.

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:34.680
The Serpent suits can’t
fight back…

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:36.850
…wearing their atmosphere
shielding devices!

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:38.510
Should they remove them?

00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:39.970
No need.

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:42.390
<i>This is Preventer Wind.</i>

00:16:43.120 --> 00:16:44.860
Zechs Marquise!

00:16:44.860 --> 00:16:46.740
I thought you were dead.

00:16:46.740 --> 00:16:48.290
<i>I was.</i>

00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:51.740
<i>But, I find that I can’t
sleep in my grave…</i>

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:54.700
<i>…while Treize’s spirit is
still roaming about.</i>

00:16:56.510 --> 00:16:59.280
<i>I heard about you from Quinze…</i>

00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:00.620
<i>…Dekim Barton.</i>

00:17:00.620 --> 00:17:02.870
<i>Surrender and disarm
yourselves at once!</i>

00:17:03.970 --> 00:17:05.960
Shoot us if you dare.

00:17:06.130 --> 00:17:07.420
What?

00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:10.170
If you fire at us,
you’ll quickly realize…

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:12.550
…that these Serpents aren’t
our last resort.

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:13.670
<i>Damn you!</i>

00:17:13.670 --> 00:17:16.530
Didn’t Quinze tell you?

00:17:16.530 --> 00:17:19.760
I was the one who created
Operation Meteor.

00:17:20.450 --> 00:17:22.730
X-18999…

00:17:25.450 --> 00:17:26.690
That’s right.

00:17:26.690 --> 00:17:29.310
We can drop that colony
any time we wish.

00:17:30.370 --> 00:17:33.280
If you continue to insist
on interfering…

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:37.110
…we will drop X-18999
onto Earth!

00:17:38.130 --> 00:17:40.770
Drop your weapons
and surrender!

00:17:40.770 --> 00:17:42.660
Unlike Quinze…

00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:45.750
…I have no intention of
inviting you to be our leader.

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:50.080
But I’ll consider you as
a soldier under Mariemaia.

00:18:19.670 --> 00:18:21.200
Now, Earth.

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:24.400
Show me what your
true idea of justice is.

00:18:24.400 --> 00:18:27.080
Drop the colony onto Earth?!

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:28.580
Stop this at once!

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:30.560
There’s no reason to do that!

00:18:30.560 --> 00:18:31.750
Relena.

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:33.830
Please calm down.

00:18:33.830 --> 00:18:36.510
I won’t need to do this.

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:39.300
So long as all of mankind
bows before me.

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:42.680
Do you really believe the people
will bow before you?

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:46.730
Yes, because in your role
as the former Queen Relena…

00:18:46.730 --> 00:18:49.480
…you entrusted me with
the highest position…

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:50.850
…of the Earth Sphere.

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:52.020
What do you mean?

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:53.690
As the Vice Foreign Minister…

00:18:53.690 --> 00:18:56.190
…you’re trusted by the colonies.

00:18:56.190 --> 00:18:59.200
You have a much greater
level of influential power…

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:01.990
…over the people than
even you realize yourself.

00:19:01.990 --> 00:19:03.990
And that’s why you abducted me.

00:19:04.430 --> 00:19:06.740
Now you’ve got the picture.

00:19:12.040 --> 00:19:15.430
The temperature in here
is above eighty degrees.

00:19:15.430 --> 00:19:18.170
I’ll just think of it
as a big sauna.

00:19:30.540 --> 00:19:32.140
This better work.

00:19:42.530 --> 00:19:45.110
Five… four… three…

00:20:04.240 --> 00:20:07.100
It should get a bit
cooler now.

00:20:18.130 --> 00:20:19.940
Operation Meteor.

00:20:20.460 --> 00:20:23.760
That’s what they called
Gundams’ descent to Earth.

00:20:23.760 --> 00:20:26.910
But it was initially something
completely different.

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:29.370
The rotation of a colony
is increased…

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:31.710
…causing its stability in 
the Lagrange Point to fail…{Then the balancing mechanism
is destroyed at La Grange…}

00:20:31.710 --> 00:20:33.460
…hurling the colony
toward Earth.

00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:35.290
As this causes chaos
on Earth…

00:20:35.290 --> 00:20:37.290
…the Gundams are sent
to take over.

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:40.620
That’s the general outline of
the original Operation Meteor.

00:20:49.820 --> 00:20:51.590
What kept you?

00:20:51.590 --> 00:20:53.020
How about that.

00:20:53.020 --> 00:20:55.770
Our objectives ended up
being the same after all.

00:20:55.770 --> 00:20:57.400
Give me a hand.

00:20:57.400 --> 00:20:59.940
They’ve got a complex
lock on the system.

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:03.070
It’s taking time to re-establish
the colony’s stability control.

00:21:03.070 --> 00:21:03.950
Sure.

00:21:06.340 --> 00:21:08.120
We’d better hurry.

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:11.040
Looks like they’ve started
sending in troops to Earth.

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:13.460
I can’t seem to break
the final lock.

00:21:13.460 --> 00:21:16.080
We’ll have to reconnect
the lines directly.

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:19.420
Many friends that I worked
with are on this colony.

00:21:19.420 --> 00:21:21.420
When I realized Dekim’s plans…

00:21:21.420 --> 00:21:23.800
…were really the original
Operation Meteor…

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:26.430
…this is the only way I
could think of to stop him.

00:21:26.430 --> 00:21:29.600
But it’s taken me way
too long to get here.

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:30.970
How about Wufei?

00:21:30.970 --> 00:21:34.600
Did he become Mariemaia’s
soldier just to get their plans?

00:21:35.040 --> 00:21:37.270
No, he hates roundabout
approaches.

00:21:42.710 --> 00:21:44.460
Okay, we’re done.

00:21:44.460 --> 00:21:45.490
This is Duo.

00:21:47.130 --> 00:21:48.820
Are you absolutely sure?!

00:21:48.820 --> 00:21:51.530
You guys stopped
Operation Meteor?!

00:21:55.260 --> 00:21:56.710
<i>This is Wind.</i>

00:21:56.710 --> 00:21:58.210
<i>I’m destroying MO-III!</i>

00:22:14.490 --> 00:22:15.930
You were late!

00:22:15.930 --> 00:22:17.720
See you again!

00:22:23.210 --> 00:22:25.000
We were too late.

00:22:25.000 --> 00:22:26.530
Don’t worry about it.

00:22:26.530 --> 00:22:28.860
At least we were able to
save the colony.

00:22:28.860 --> 00:22:30.990
We have you completely
surrounded.

00:22:30.990 --> 00:22:32.700
Come out with your hands up.

00:22:32.700 --> 00:22:34.110
It’s over.

00:22:34.110 --> 00:22:36.290
Not necessarily.

00:22:36.290 --> 00:22:38.170
I got some mail from Quatre.

00:22:38.360 --> 00:22:40.210
<i>Quatre here.</i>

00:22:40.210 --> 00:22:44.050
<i>I’ve just redirected the resources
disposal satellite toward Earth.</i>

00:22:44.050 --> 00:22:47.790
<i>It should reach the Earth’s orbit
within twenty-four hours.</i>

00:22:47.790 --> 00:22:50.590
Duo, send Quatre a message.

00:22:50.900 --> 00:22:54.600
Tell him to send Wing Zero in
the HES-88 direction.

00:22:54.600 --> 00:22:55.890
You kidding?!

00:22:55.890 --> 00:22:57.930
I’ll pick up Wing Zero in space.

00:22:57.930 --> 00:23:00.230
It’ll save time that way.

00:23:00.230 --> 00:23:01.400
Open the door!

00:23:01.400 --> 00:23:02.190
Open up!

00:23:02.790 --> 00:23:05.610
You can take the shuttle
in the fourth hangar.

00:23:05.610 --> 00:23:08.800
Duo, I have another favor.

00:23:08.800 --> 00:23:10.450
That’s not like you.

00:23:10.450 --> 00:23:12.970
Suddenly asking me
all these favors.

00:23:12.970 --> 00:23:14.590
Hit me!

00:23:14.590 --> 00:23:16.090
Have you gone crazy?!

00:23:16.090 --> 00:23:16.910
Never mind!

00:23:16.910 --> 00:23:18.500
Tear down the door!

00:23:18.500 --> 00:23:19.790
Hurry up!

00:23:19.790 --> 00:23:21.910
Well, you asked for it.

00:23:22.350 --> 00:23:24.370
I’ll give you my best punch!

00:23:28.820 --> 00:23:30.710
Why in the…

00:23:30.710 --> 00:23:32.260
For our own good.

00:23:32.260 --> 00:23:33.640
That’s one for one.

00:23:35.240 --> 00:23:36.680
He’s all yours.

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:37.920
Right.

00:23:43.210 --> 00:23:44.400
Don’t worry.

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:46.070
I’ve taken care of them.

00:23:46.070 --> 00:23:48.560
But they prevented the
colony’s instability.

00:23:50.130 --> 00:23:51.320
Stop!

00:23:51.570 --> 00:23:53.270
Freeze! Wait!

00:24:03.710 --> 00:24:07.130
<i>I feel love, reflection</i>

00:24:07.130 --> 00:24:10.380
<i>mitsumekaesu hitomi ni</i>

00:24:07.130 --> 00:24:10.380
<i>The reflection of your eyes
looking at me</i>

00:24:10.380 --> 00:24:13.430
<i>egaite haruka na</i>

00:24:10.380 --> 00:24:13.430
<i>Is etched in my mind
as an everlasting</i>

00:24:13.430 --> 00:24:20.230
<i>Never-ending story</i>

00:24:33.450 --> 00:24:37.030
<i>kanashimi mo itami mo</i>

00:24:33.450 --> 00:24:37.030
<i>Beating these wings
with all my might</i>

00:24:37.030 --> 00:24:40.200
<i>furikiru you ni habataku</i>

00:24:37.030 --> 00:24:40.200
<i>To shake off all sadness,
shake off all pain</i>

00:24:40.200 --> 00:24:43.080
<i>anata ga kureta tsubasa wo</i>

00:24:40.200 --> 00:24:43.080
<i>These wings will always
be spread across my heart</i>

00:24:43.080 --> 00:24:46.880
<i>kono mune ni hirogete</i>

00:24:43.080 --> 00:24:46.880
<i>These wings that I received
from you</i>

00:24:46.880 --> 00:24:53.260
<i>aa kakegaenai ai no kodou wo</i>

00:24:46.880 --> 00:24:53.260
<i>As painful as it may be
and as upset as I may get</i>

00:24:53.260 --> 00:25:00.020
<i>setsunaku kuruoshiku kanjite itai</i>

00:24:53.260 --> 00:25:00.020
<i>I hope to keep feeling
this precious love beating</i>

00:25:00.020 --> 00:25:03.310
<i>I feel love, reflection</i>

00:25:03.310 --> 00:25:06.730
<i>atsuku yume wo kasanete</i>

00:25:03.310 --> 00:25:06.730
<i>We’ll have many passionate
dreams together</i>

00:25:06.730 --> 00:25:10.030
<i>ayamachi osorezu ni</i>

00:25:06.730 --> 00:25:10.030
<i>Unafraid to make mistakes</i>

00:25:10.030 --> 00:25:13.280
<i>motomeau seishun</i>

00:25:10.030 --> 00:25:13.280
<i>We’ll look to each other</i>

00:25:13.280 --> 00:25:16.570
<i>I feel love, reflection</i>

00:25:16.570 --> 00:25:19.740
<i>mitsumekaesu hitomi ni</i>

00:25:16.570 --> 00:25:19.740
<i>The reflection of your eyes
looking at me</i>

00:25:19.740 --> 00:25:22.910
<i>egaite haruka na</i>

00:25:19.740 --> 00:25:22.910
<i>Is etched in my mind
as an everlasting</i>

00:25:22.910 --> 00:25:29.920
<i>Never-ending story</i>

00:25:49.400 --> 00:25:52.360
Next Episode

00:25:50.520 --> 00:25:52.360
After Colony 197.

00:25:53.290 --> 00:25:55.780
Having taken over Earth…

00:25:55.780 --> 00:25:58.860
…Mariemaia was ready
to perform an endless waltz.

00:25:59.300 --> 00:26:02.080
While pursuing an
everlasting future…

00:26:02.080 --> 00:26:05.540
…the men spread destruction
and prepare for tragedy.

00:26:05.700 --> 00:26:09.290
But this results in
a final moment…

00:26:09.290 --> 00:26:11.940
…when lost souls are
called back.

00:26:11.940 --> 00:26:15.760
Next, on the final episode of
<i>Gundam Wing: Endless Waltz</i>.

00:26:15.760 --> 00:26:19.430
Return to Forever
